From d71568e347b2e2dc3dfb4977a328d6ea5f11cb08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <winshyon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:54:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] git: remote, Split fetch and push code out of remote.go.
 Fixes #1518

Fetching and pushing share very little code, yet both lived in the same
1.7k-line file. Move the fetch-only declarations to remote_fetch.go and
the push-only ones to remote_push.go, and do the same for their tests
(remote_fetch_test.go, remote_push_test.go).

remote.go keeps the Remote type, its constructor, the exported sentinel
errors, List/ListContext, and the helpers used by both directions or by
other files: referenceStorageFromRefs, usableRemoteRef,
unstorableRefName, newClient, transportProtocol and isFastForward.

This is a pure move: every declaration is carried over byte for byte,
in its original relative order. The only edit is splitting the shared
const block, since maxHavesToVisitPerRef is used by fetch alone while
peeledSuffix is shared. No behaviour changes.
